<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Evripidis Bakirtzis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1947</span> · Also known as Euripidis Bakirtzis</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Evripidis Bakirtzis was a Greek army officer known as the 'Red Colonel' for his left-wing views. A veteran of the Balkan and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asia-minor">Asia Minor</a> wars, he joined the resistance during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> occupation and in March 1944 became the first president of the Political Committee of National Liberation (PEEA), set up by EAM. He died in internal exile on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ikaria">Ikaria</a> in 1947.</p></div>
